          "cachedResultName": "llava-phi3:latest"
        },
        "text": "=Write a description of the image, and then give an appropriate new name to the image based on the description. Don't imagine anything yourself.\nWrite new name instead of the old {{ $json.name }} field and keep {{ $json.id }} field as it is.\nFollow the next 5 rules for image naming:\n\n1. Field \"name\" should be readable in english. \n2. All words must be separated by underscores.\n3. No digits allowed at all.\n4. All names should not contain whitespaces at all.\n5. Do not mention names of any countries and cities and castles in \"name\" field if it's not written on an image.\n6. All names must be unique.\n7. All names must be renamed with a new name.\nInside the $json.message.content field must have the following JSON format:\n{\n  \"id\": {{ $json.id }},\n  \"name\": new name, plus file extension,\n\"description\": your description of an image, 100 words maximum. in description include objects like trees, sea, lake, buildings... which you can find on image. If there any inscriptions on the image, include it in the name and in description field.Don't make assumptions in which country or city a photo was taken unless you clearly can identify it. Don't give names like \"Effiel Tower\" or \"Sagrada Familia\" to buildings on images.,\n  \"link_to_download_image\": {{ $json.webViewLink }}\n}\n\n",
        "simplify": false,
        "options": {
          "low_vram": true,
          "num_batch": 256
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.ollama",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2160,
        80
      ],
      "id": "f5278169-8a29-4f46-a789-6067c607de79",
      "name": "Analyze image",
      "alwaysOutputData": true,
      "credentials": {
        "ollamaApi": {
          "id": "b01aHzdDX6mSkPej",
          "name": "Ollama account"
        }
